WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.660
The beloved actress who gave away the entire
plot of her movie on national television?

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.700
The actor from a massive film franchise spoiling
their character's death?

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:11.630
And, which actor got fired for his mistake?

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.950
Keep watching to be shocked about these spoilers!

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:17.430
David Prowse played Darth Vader in the original
Star Wars trilogy.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.949
Or at least, he was the guy in the Vader costume
and helmet.

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:25.720
James Earl Jones provided the voice, and Sebastian
Shaw played the unmasked villain at the end

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.369
of Return of the Jedi.

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:32.649
Prowse's image wasn't as well-known as those
of co-stars like Mark Hamill or Harrison Ford.

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:37.920
But, the first wave of Star Wars mania in
1978 was so huge that a Prowse meet-and-greet

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.850
in Berkeley, California, drew 1,000 people.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:45.149
The British actor delighted the audience at
the event with stories about his career and

00:00:45.149 --> 00:00:49.190
the first Star Wars movie, including news
that a sequel was in pre-production.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:53.440
Prowse promised that Star Wars II would feature
a lightsaber battle between Luke Skywalker

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.440
and Darth Vader.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:58.670
And then he said that Darth Vader would reveal
to Luke that he was his father.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:02.449
Star Wars II became The Empire Strikes Back,
of course, and it featured the exact same

00:01:02.449 --> 00:01:04.820
twist Prowse had spoiled years before.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:06.807
"That's impossible!"

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:11.060
Prowse wasn't the only cast member from The
Empire Strikes Back to spoil the movie.

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:16.229
Billy Dee Williams, who played the irresistibly
roguish Lando Calrissian, spilled another

00:01:16.229 --> 00:01:21.810
Star Wars secret, but on a much higher-profile
venue: NBC's long-running morning show Today.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:26.920
To be fair, Williams had to reveal that Lando
wasn't really a bad guy, just a crafty manipulator.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.749
He seemed to get a little defensive when the
interviewer labeled his character as evil,

00:01:30.749 --> 00:01:31.749
and decided to interject.

00:01:31.749 --> 00:01:32.749
"He's not evil.

00:01:32.749 --> 00:01:34.820
He's just a guy caught in a situation."

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:39.130
In the grand scheme of Star Wars spoilers,
it's a pretty minor reveal — but on the

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:43.720
other hand, it did ruin a pretty significant
plot twist for anyone who watched the interview

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:44.869
before the movie.

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:50.569
Like most time travel movies, The Time Traveler's
Wife has a complicated premise.

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:54.560
That makes for a fine line, then, between
explaining a movie's plot and spoiling the

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.990
movie entirely.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:02:00.869
The Time Traveler's Wife star Rachel McAdams
accidentally crossed that line while promoting

00:02:00.869 --> 00:02:02.939
the film on the Daily Show.

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:07.039
Host Jon Stewart asked how far outside the
present the story's time-traveling husband

00:02:07.039 --> 00:02:09.159
was able to journey, and McAdams explained,

00:02:09.159 --> 00:02:13.930
"He goes as far as his own childhood ... He
goes forward as far as his own death."

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:18.540
After a moment of silence in which McAdams
realized what she'd done, Stewart replied,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:19.540
"Whoa!

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.069
He knows how he's gonna die before he dies?"

00:02:22.069 --> 00:02:24.440
McAdams, a little embarrassed, sighed,

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.010
"Now we've ruined everything."

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:31.150
It's probably worth mentioning that the movie
was based on the 2003 bestseller of the same

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.550
name, and fans of the book most definitely
were already aware of the title character's

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:36.550
fate.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:40.778
Still, promoting a film romance by spoiling
a death is usually not the best way to go.

00:02:41.266 --> 00:02:45.110
Sylvester Stallone produced — and earned
a Best Supporting Actor nomination — for

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:49.650
his role in Creed, a Rocky franchise spinoff
that helped revive the blockbuster series

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:50.980
he created in the '70s.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:57.610
In 2014, he tweeted out an artsy, sentimental
photo of the filmmaking process behind the

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:01.150
film with the caption: "Where the screenwriting
is done."

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:04.980
The picture showed a pair of glasses, some
handwritten notes...and the last page of the

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:06.379
script for Creed.

00:03:06.379 --> 00:03:10.200
The page was upside down, but if fans wanted
to know how the movie ended, all they had

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:12.519
to do was flip the photo and zoom in a little.

00:03:13.519 --> 00:03:16.879
Game of Thrones fans were thrilled when it
was announced that Ian McShane from Deadwood

00:03:16.879 --> 00:03:21.340
would join the cast of HBO's epic fantasy
series in its sixth season.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:25.640
In an interview on BBC Breakfast about his
role as Brother Ray, however, he gave away

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.489
a little too much.

00:03:27.489 --> 00:03:28.489
McShane said,

00:03:28.489 --> 00:03:31.310
"I bring back a much-loved character who everybody
thinks is dead."

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:36.010
Vanity Fair connected the dots and determined
that McShane meant the Hound, as actor Rory

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.950
McCann had been spotted on set.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:43.290
Informed he'd upset some people with his casual
plot spoiling, McShane offered Game of Thrones

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.850
fans a verbal eyeroll.

00:03:44.850 --> 00:03:46.299
He told the Telegraph,

00:03:46.299 --> 00:03:49.420
"You say the slightest thing and the internet
goes ape.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:53.189
I was accused of giving the plot away, but
I just think get a f--- life."

00:03:54.024 --> 00:03:59.560
Logan marked the end of Hugh Jackman's 17-year
journey playing Wolverine across eight X-Men

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:00.560
films.

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.659
And while the X-franchise will continue with
the heroes played by younger actors, Wolverine

00:04:04.659 --> 00:04:09.470
doesn't really age, so there was essentially
only one way that the character — and Jackman's

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.950
portrayal of him — could end: with Wolverine's
death.

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:16.780
Still, it wasn't cool when Jackman, on the
week Logan hit theaters, told Entertainment

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:18.230
Weekly that's how it ended.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.230
He revealed,

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:22.990
"In the end, he must give his life to save
someone else ... I thought that was really

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:24.000
powerful."

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:28.020
He wasn't wrong, although it might have been
even more powerful if he'd managed to keep

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:28.636
it to himself.

00:04:29.325 --> 00:04:34.160
Millions of people were excited for Rogue
One, the first in a planned series of standalone

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.140
Star Wars spinoff movies.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:37.330
Among the most pumped?

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:41.380
The people who took time out of their lives
to attend Star Wars Celebration Europe, where

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:46.240
actor Jiang Wen blew the Rogue One ending
for everyone watching the conference.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:50.770
Wen portrayed Baze Malbus, one of the members
of the ragtag group who comes together to

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.530
steal the plans for the Death Star to stop
the Empire.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:58.450
Baze heroically dies in his mission, which
Wen mentioned during a livestreamed Star Wars

00:04:58.450 --> 00:04:59.850
Celebration panel.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:04.260
He would've revealed more details had panel
host Gwendolyn Christie not cut him off, warning,

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.140
"I think you've got to leave it there."

00:05:06.592 --> 00:05:11.740
By the time Avengers: Infinity War hit theaters
in 2018, Mark Ruffalo had played the famously

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.440
green-skinned muscle man the Hulk in five
Marvel Cinematic Universe movies.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:20.570
But somehow, he wound up leaking significant
details of two of those highly anticipated

00:05:20.570 --> 00:05:23.330
films before they were released for the public.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:28.350
Infinity War is the first in a two-film Avengers
finale and features a brutal and sad twist

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:33.820
ending in which intergalactic villain Thanos
snaps half of all life out of existence, including

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:35.430
many of the Avengers.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:40.430
It's unbelievable, and it's even more unbelievable
that Ruffalo told the world such events would

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:44.880
happen during an appearance on Good Morning
America nearly a year before Infinity War

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:46.910
would arrive at cineplexes.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:47.910
Ruffalo teased,

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.250
"Wait til you see this next one.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:51.250
Everybody dies."

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.250
"Dude!

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:53.250
Dude!"

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.250
"Not everybody.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.250
No."

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:59.300
Not long after the Good Morning America incident,
Ruffalo attended the premiere of the 2017

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:03.590
MCU entry Thor: Ragnarok in which he co-stars
as the Hulk.

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:07.760
At the premiere, he accidentally shared the
movie with anyone watching his Instagram live

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:08.760
feed.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:12.810
By forgetting to switch off Insta before putting
his phone in his pocket, Ruffalo accidentally

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:16.303
streamed the first 20 minutes of the movie's
audio over the internet.

00:06:16.755 --> 00:06:21.440
Tom Holland is a versatile actor and international
celebrity who does two things more than anything

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.860
else in his busy career.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:27.710
He plays Spider-Man whenever the MCU requires
him to do so, and he routinely spoils sensitive

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:31.630
or top-secret details about those same MCU
films.

00:06:31.630 --> 00:06:37.220
In June 2018, Holland put in an appearance
at ACE Seattle Comic Con and posted a video

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:42.380
to his Instagram page to calm down fans eager
for details about his upcoming second Spider-Man

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.380
film.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:47.230
Tom said these words before ironically and
accidentally revealing the movie's name:

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:52.070
"I wanted to apologize because there's no
real revelations coming out this weekend about

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.020
'Spider-Man 2,' [...] I got the new script.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:55.710
I'm super excited to read it.

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.010
It's gonna be great!"

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:01.760
The funniest part is that Holland said all
this while holding up the iPad upon which

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:07.850
he was reading the script, with the not-yet-public
title, Spider-Man: Far From Home very visible.

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:11.690
Here's a spoiler alert for Avengers: Infinity
War — Spider-Man dies in the end.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:15.950
A crowd filled a theater at the ArcLight in
Los Angeles for a special early screening

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:20.950
of that film hosted by directors Joe and Anthony
Russo, along with some of the cast members.

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:24.120
Holland came out on stage and quipped, "I'm
alive!"

00:07:24.120 --> 00:07:28.670
Though obviously confused about whether he
was walking out before or after the screening,

00:07:28.670 --> 00:07:31.510
Holland coyly but clearly revealed his character's
fate.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.390
"That was a test right?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:34.950
There's, uh, nobody back there?"

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:35.785
"Yes, you've passed."

00:07:36.127 --> 00:07:40.370
Plenty of superhero movies are also origin
stories that lay the groundwork for future

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:44.820
sequels by showing how a regular individual
acquires their superpowers and embraces their

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:48.181
extraordinary lot in life.

00:07:48.181 --> 00:07:51.930
Aquaman, the 2018 mega-blockbuster entry in
DC Comics' cinematic universe, features Jason

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:57.311
Momoa as the title lord of the seas, reprising
the role he plays in 2017's team-up movie

00:07:57.311 --> 00:07:58.530
Justice League.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:02.961
At the time, filmgoers might not all have
anticipated Aquaman to be an origin story

00:08:02.961 --> 00:08:05.590
that takes place before the events of Justice
League.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:09.450
But they soon found out as much, thanks to
an excitable Momoa sharing a little too much

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:13.990
about the movie — particularly its ending
and his character's arc — during his promotional

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:15.610
rounds for Justice League.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:17.100
As he told SFX Magazine,

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.310
"He's not even really Aquaman yet.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:21.050
He's not the King of the Seven Seas.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.990
We don't really get there until my solo movie,
at the end.

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:25.530
Really, it's a huge growth for me.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.310
It's a gigantic arc for Arthur Curry."

00:08:28.310 --> 00:08:32.400
Guardians of the Galaxy was something of a
surprise hit in 2014, because it's based on

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:37.099
more obscure source material than previously
successful MCU outings like Iron Man, Captain

00:08:37.099 --> 00:08:38.439
America, and Thor.

00:08:38.439 --> 00:08:42.319
Only relatively hardcore comics fans knew
what to expect from Guardians.

00:08:42.319 --> 00:08:46.519
Hardly anybody could predict how events would
unfold in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2,

00:08:46.519 --> 00:08:48.730
which hit theaters in 2017.

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:52.790
The sequel adds mysterious new characters
to the mix, including Ayesha, played by Australian

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:54.800
actor Elizabeth Debicki.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:59.210
While discussing and promoting the movie at
San Diego Comic-Con in the summer of 2016

00:08:59.210 --> 00:09:03.819
which was a year before the film would see
release, Debicki laid out most of Ayesha's

00:09:03.819 --> 00:09:04.819
arc.

00:09:04.819 --> 00:09:08.680
Unfortunately she also included one of the
film's twists — she isn't one of the good

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:09.680
guys.

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:14.050
In fact, Ayesha is a villain who tricks the
protagonists into fighting on her behalf.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:16.790
As she told Gizmodo at San Diego Comic Con,

00:09:16.790 --> 00:09:19.300
"Ayesha is this leader of the Sovereign people.

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:23.209
She enlists the Guardians to help her fight
a sort of galactic beast.

00:09:23.209 --> 00:09:26.209
It's all going swimmingly until it all turns
very very sour.

00:09:26.209 --> 00:09:29.930
Let's just say it goes from amiable to not-so-amiable
quite quickly."

00:09:30.418 --> 00:09:34.149
Actor Rodri Martin works primarily in Spanish-language
media.

00:09:34.149 --> 00:09:39.079
In 2021, he landed a very plum gig — performing
the dub for actor Evan Peters in the Spanish

00:09:39.079 --> 00:09:42.470
version of the Disney+ MCU series WandaVision.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:46.879
Peters' appearance on the show as Pietro Maximoff,
who was presumed dead, is a mega-surprise

00:09:46.879 --> 00:09:49.970
in the complicated, slow-boil world of WandaVision.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:54.740
According to Cinexcepcion, Martin revealed
his casting on Twitter ahead of Pietro's big

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:59.040
Episode 5 reveal, which violated Martin's
confidentiality agreement with Disney and

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:00.040
Marvel.

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:04.620
Martin also told Twitter that he'd be dubbing
Peters' lines in future MCU projects — which

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:08.889
means, ironically, at that point Martin either
didn't really know how WandaVision ends or

00:10:08.889 --> 00:10:13.009
was trying to throw fans off the track of
figuring out the real deal with Pietro.

00:10:13.009 --> 00:10:17.730
The source states that for potentially spoiling
multiple projects and ignoring contract language,

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:22.250
Disney terminated Martin and replaced him
with Manuel Gimeno, the actor who performed

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:24.750
the dubs for Charlie Cox in Marvel's Daredevil
series.

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:30.509
While the Star Wars prequels weren't as well-received
as the original trilogy, there are some undeniably

00:10:30.509 --> 00:10:35.470
great elements of the films — such as the
always terrific Samuel L. Jackson as a Jedi

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.170
named Mace Windu.

00:10:37.170 --> 00:10:41.000
Prior to the release of the final prequel,
Revenge of the Sith, Jackson sat for an interview

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.319
with Now Playing.

00:10:42.319 --> 00:10:45.819
When asked what Windu would be doing in the
film, Jackson answered, "Dying!"

00:10:45.819 --> 00:10:49.779
He then added that he couldn't go into too
much detail, but that his character would

00:10:49.779 --> 00:10:51.339
face "an awesome death."

00:10:51.339 --> 00:10:56.259
Of course, hardcore Star Wars fans were already
aware that the Jedi faced near-total extinction

00:10:56.259 --> 00:11:00.339
during the events leading up to the original
trilogy, so Windu's death wasn't totally a

00:11:00.339 --> 00:11:01.339
surprise.

00:11:01.339 --> 00:11:05.660
Still, having it confirmed this way counts
as something of a disturbance in the Force.

